{"text": "MEMO TO PAYROLL FILE\nClient: Thistledown Bakery Supply, Inc. (EIN 31-1940662)\nPrepared by: Noor Hadjiev, Hadjiev & Marlowe Payroll Accountants, Columbus, Ohio\nDate: May 12, 2026\nRe: Employee Terrence D. Holloway, emp. no. 00417 - two withholding orders received the same week\n1. Employee\nHolloway, Terrence D.; SSN 237-27-5134; DOB 9/30/1990; warehouse lead, hired 08/14/2019; paid biweekly, $26.40 an hour. Home address on the orders is 618 Sullivant Avenue, Columbus, OH 43223, which does not match our file (2240 Gantz Rd Lot 31, Grove City). Wendell Cray in HR will ask him which is right; do not send anything to either address until then.\n2. Orders received\n• Income Withholding for Support (IWO), Form OMB 0970-0154, issued April 29, 2026 by the Franklin County Court of Common Pleas, Domestic Relations and Juvenile, case no. 24 JU 03 2291, SETS case 7049336118. Obligee: Brianna Sepulveda. Child: Jaylen Holloway, born 03/17/2019. Current child support $612.00 per month; cash medical support $41.50 per month; arrears payment $122.40 per month on past-due support of $8,930.17. Total $775.90 per month, which the order converts to $358.11 biweekly.\n• Creditor garnishment, Franklin County Municipal Court, case 2026 CVF 011872, served 5/1/2026. Judgment creditor Candlewood Credit Recovery LLC, assignee of Olentangy Motor Credit (deficiency on a repossessed 2018 Chevrolet Malibu). Judgment balance $6,204.88 plus costs.\n3. Priority and calculation (per pay period)\nChild support comes first (Ohio Rev. Code § 3121.03). The CCPA limit for support is 55% of disposable earnings here because he supports no second family and is more than 12 weeks in arrears; see 15 U.S.C. § 1673.\nStep\tAmount\nGross (80 hrs)\t$2,112.00\nFederal, FICA, state, city tax\t(431.87)\nDisposable earnings\t$1,680.13\nSupport withheld (IWO)\t358.11\nProcessing fee kept by employer\t$2.00\n25% cap for creditor garnishment\t$420.03\nAlready taken by support\t358.11\nRemaining for Candlewood\t$61.92\n\nSo each check: 358.11 to support, $61.92 to the creditor, until the judgment is paid or we are told to stop. Start with the pay date of May 22.\n4. Remittance\nSupport goes by EFT to Ohio Child Support Payment Central within 7 days of each pay date, using the SETS case number and the employee's SSN. The EFT is drawn on the payroll account at Scioto Commons Bank, routing 080391137, account ending -8816. The creditor's share goes by check to the clerk, memo \"2026 CVF 011872 / T. Holloway\".\n5. Open items\n• Mr. Holloway told Wendell he filed Chapter 13 in March (he gave case no. 2:26-bk-51077). If that is right, the creditor garnishment must stop, but the support order does not. Hold the $61.92 in the liability account until we see the notice from the Trustee. Do not discuss the bankruptcy with his supervisor.\n• He also asked that Jaylen be added to his medical plan; that is an HR matter, not payroll, but the IWO has a medical support box checked. Ms. Sepulveda's attorney called HR twice; refer any calls to me at 614-555-0173 or noor@hadjievmarlowe.example.\n• New Form W-4 not needed.\nNH", "kind": "Rich Text document", "detail": "501 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Holloway, Terrence D.", "Brianna Sepulveda", "Mr. Holloway", "Wendell", "Jaylen", "Ms. Sepulveda"], "companies": ["Thistledown Bakery Supply, Inc.", "Hadjiev & Marlowe Payroll Accountants", "Franklin County Court of Common Pleas", "Franklin County Municipal Court", "Candlewood Credit Recovery LLC", "Olentangy Motor Credit", "Chevrolet Malibu", "Ohio Rev. Code", "Ohio Child Support Payment Central", "Scioto Commons Bank", "hadjievmarlowe.example"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 1.1000000014901161, "modelMs": 35389.199999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "po